<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ragamuffin War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1835–1845</span> · Also known as Farroupilha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ragamuffin War, or Farroupilha, was a republican and separatist revolt in the southern Brazilian province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande-do-sul">Rio Grande do Sul</a>, lasting from 1835 to 1845. It was the longest of the provincial rebellions that shook the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> during and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/regency-period-brazil">Regency period</a>. It ended with a negotiated settlement under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a>'s government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ragamuffin-war.jpg" alt="Ragamuffin War" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guilherme Litran · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carga_de_Cavalaria_by_Guilherme_Litran.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
